// ===========================================================================
// games/sonic4/data/sound/mt_bank.emp — the Moving-Trucks song bank (bank 1): the songs
// and their FM patch banks, placed NATIVELY, and the ONE list of them
// ===========================================================================
// This module is both halves of the bank-1 song region (song bank 2, step 1, 2026-09-28):
//   * the ROM build places its `mt_bank` section at the `Song_MovingTrucks` map row, right
//     after the engine-table head (`soundbankhead.emp`) in the `sound_bank` window, with
//     every song and patch bank a real linker label (`Song_S2_EHZ`, `S2_EHZ_Patches`, ...);
//   * sigil's seam-2 (`emit_sound_blob`) lowers the SAME file standalone to measure the
//     section's length, from which it predicts `Sfx_33` (the SFX block packs right after
//     this section) and folds the SFX pointers against that prediction. The fold gate
//     (`[sound.fold-vs-placement]`) refuses a build whose placed `Sfx_33` disagrees.
// Before step 1 the ROM build embedded seam-2's opaque `mt_bank_body*.bin` through a
// second module (`mt_bank_blob.emp`, deleted), so no song label was visible to the link
// and the song tables had to live here, inside seam-2's standalone lowering, where a
// song in another bank could never be named. The tables now live with their only reader's
// data (`SongTable`/`SongPatchTable`, in `sfx_bank_blob.emp`, after the SFX block).
//
// TWO LOWERINGS, ONE SPELLING. Every `embed` path below is AEON-ROOT relative, which is
// what the ROM build resolves; seam-2 picks its base from these literals (sigil
// SONG-BANK-2-EMBED-ROOT, merge 116aa23e) and refuses a mix of spellings
// (`[sound.mt-embed-mixed]`), a path that names two different files
// (`[sound.mt-embed-ambiguous]`) and a computed path (`[sound.mt-embed-computed]`). Keep
// them plain string literals, all spelled from the root.
//
// DO NOT RENAME `Song_MovingTrucks` AND KEEP IT THE FIRST ITEM. It is the map row that
// places this section and the label sigil's fold gate compares against its prediction;
// that gate silently skips a label it cannot find (sigil SOUND-FOLD-GATE-SILENT-SKIP,
// booked), so a rename would turn the gate off without a word.
//
// Shape input: `-D DEBUG=0|1`. Plain shape (DEBUG=0) carries Moving Trucks and Sonic 2's
// Emerald Hill and Chemical Plant; DEBUG shape (DEBUG=1) adds DrumTest and HCZ2. Both
// shapes emit the SAME data items, the DEBUG-only ones folding to `Data.empty` (zero
// bytes, label still defined) when DEBUG=0.
//
// The invariants this bank enforces:
//   * No-straddle: the section's `bank: $8000` property is an always-on no-straddle link
//     assert, so every song and patch here shares ONE bank.
//   * Co-residency with the engine-table head (the sequencer reads FM pitch/log-volume/
//     opcode tables window-relative from the bank head, so a song must sit in a bank that
//     starts with the head). Held by three checks together, not by an `ensure` here: the
//     head is 0x8000-aligned (sigil `section_align` `SoundTablesZ80_Head`), seam-2 refuses
//     a predicted section base outside the head's window (`mt_bank_room`), and the fold gate
//     requires the placed `Song_MovingTrucks` to equal that prediction; the no-straddle
//     property carries the rest of the section. The nine `ensure(bankid(X) ==
//     bankid("MovingTrucks_Bank_Start"))` lines that stated it were deleted in step 1:
//     `MovingTrucks_Bank_Start` is a seam-2-only carrier label, and the ROM build (which
//     now lowers this module too) refuses an extern it cannot resolve.
//   * Pitch-contiguity: contiguous BY CONSTRUCTION (items in a section always emit
//     back-to-back, no auto-pad, §4.3) + `ensure(SongBlob.len == MT_PITCHTAB_OFFSET, …)`.
//   * Trailing pads: EXPLICIT self-adjusting pad items (`.emp` sections never auto-pad,
//     §4.3); see the comments at each pad below.
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT PORTED: the `_End` labels (`Song_MovingTrucks_End`, etc.); every
// consumer reads a blob's `.len` (comptime), never an end-minus-start.
//
// Re-pin note (PROVENANCE): the `$30B1` pitch-table offset is pinned; a song regeneration
// must re-verify it (the `MT_PITCHTAB_OFFSET` ensure below is the CI-visible tripwire).
// ===========================================================================

module games.sonic4.mt_bank_blob

// --- the six stream blobs (generated .bin). Bound to `const` first
// so each `.len` is a readable comptime int (the `data K = embed(...)`
// readability gate — the const both emits AND measures, dac_samples.emp
// precedent). ---
const SongBlob      = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/song_movingtrucks.bin")              // 12465 B ($30B1)
const PitchBlob     = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/movingtrucks_pitchtable_stream.bin") // 264 B ($108)
const PatchesBlob   = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/movingtrucks_patches.bin")           // 800 B ($320)
const DrumTestBlob  = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/song_drumtest.bin")                  // 82 B ($52)  (DEBUG member)
const Hcz2Blob      = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/song_hcz2.bin")                      // 6511 B ($196F) (DEBUG member)
const Hcz2PatchBlob = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/hcz2_patches.bin")                   // 128 B ($80)  (DEBUG member)
// Sonic 2 EHZ + CPZ (S2CLIP-REGION-MUSIC step 4), every shape. Generated by
// song_s2_ehz_cpz.py and committed; tools/test_smps_import.py holds them equal to a
// fresh run. Each carries its OWN FM patch bank (Sonic 2's song-local voices).
const S2EhzBlob      = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/song_s2_ehz.bin")                   // 2528 B ($9E0)
const S2EhzPatchBlob = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/s2_ehz_patches.bin")                // 288 B ($120)
const S2CpzBlob      = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/song_s2_cpz.bin")                   // 3613 B ($E1D)
const S2CpzPatchBlob = embed("games/sonic4/data/sound/s2_cpz_patches.bin")                // 192 B ($C0)

// Length-guard note: only the song's length is CI-pinned (via the
// MT_PITCHTAB_OFFSET ensure below, which is load-bearing — a wrong song
// length detunes the whole song). The other five blob lengths are NOT
// individually `ensure`d here: they're sanity-known (see the comments above)
// but pinning every one would just add regen churn with no guard they don't
// already get for free — the section's `bank: $8000` no-straddle assert
// catches any gross length blowup, and the byte-identity harness (Task 6)
// catches anything subtler.

// The song ids and the table order they index live with the tables (`SongTable` /
// `SongPatchTable`, sfx_bank_blob.emp); nothing in this module depends on an id.


// The generator-baked header offset (song_movingtrucks header pitchtable_ptr
// = packed song length). Re-pin on song regeneration; this ensure is the detune
// guard — a mismatch means the header disagrees with the layout below (a pad byte
// between the song and the pitch table would shift every pitch lookup one byte
// early = the whole song plays a semitone flat).
const MT_PITCHTAB_OFFSET = $30B1
ensure(SongBlob.len == MT_PITCHTAB_OFFSET,
    "MT pitch table not contiguous with the song: song len != header's pitchtable_ptr — a pad byte would detune the whole song")

// --- SFX-base 8-alignment pad size (package 3 fix — see the _sfx_align item
// in the section below for the full story). The running length of everything
// this section emits before the pad, mirrored comptime: the
// three always-on blobs + the DEBUG members + their self-adjusting odd-length
// align-2 pads ((len % 2) is exactly that conditional pad's size). The pad
// rounds it to ≡ 0 (mod 8); with the section base ≡ 0 (mod 8) (the head is
// rounded to 8 in soundbankhead.emp and the `sound_bank` anchor is 0x8000-aligned),
// the section END — the SFX block's base — is then ≡ 0 (mod 8) by construction,
// for any song regen or shape. (Until song bank 2 step 1 the two song pointer
// tables, 8*SONG_COUNT B, followed this pad; they now follow the SFX block.)
const _MT_DEBUG_EXTRA = if DEBUG == 1 { DrumTestBlob.len + (DrumTestBlob.len % 2) + Hcz2Blob.len + (Hcz2Blob.len % 2) + Hcz2PatchBlob.len } else { 0 }
const _MT_S2_LEN = S2EhzBlob.len + (S2EhzBlob.len % 2) + S2EhzPatchBlob.len + S2CpzBlob.len + (S2CpzBlob.len % 2) + S2CpzPatchBlob.len
const _MT_PRETABLE_LEN = SongBlob.len + PitchBlob.len + PatchesBlob.len + _MT_S2_LEN + _MT_DEBUG_EXTRA
// 1..8, never 0: the pad is the section's LAST item, and a zero-length item there would
// leave an empty label at the section's end, which is the SFX block head's address
// (`Sfx_33`, the next section). Sigil's fold gate requires each folded head to lead its
// section (SOUND-FOLD-GATE-SILENT-SKIP, sigil merge a8b1d9a5); a label tied with the head
// is the ambiguity that rule exists for, so none is left there. Costs 8 B only when the
// songs already end 8-aligned.
const MT_TAIL_PAD = 8 - (_MT_PRETABLE_LEN % 8)
ensure(MT_TAIL_PAD >= 1 && MT_TAIL_PAD <= 8, "MT tail pad out of 1..8")

// READING THE `.asm` CITATIONS BELOW. They are PROVENANCE for a byte-identity port, not a
// live second copy: every file they name is deleted. The seven Moving-Trucks AS sources
// (song_table.asm, song_drumtest.asm, song_hcz2.asm and their siblings) went in `19fce50b`;
// games/sonic4/main.asm went in `f7405d63` and its placement duties are now
// games/sonic4/map.toml. Recover any of them at that commit's parent —
//     git show 19fce50b^:games/sonic4/data/sound/song_table.asm
// — and the line numbers below land. The claims are true about those revisions; naming the
// revision is what stops the coordinates rotting the way scene_dsl.emp's did.
//
// ONE bank: $8000 section = the .asm's `align $8000` (main.asm:221) + all
// four straddle/window-top fatals (song_table.asm:74/82/93/111). Items emit
// contiguously (§4.3 no-auto-pad) = the .asm's hand-maintained contiguity
// comments made structural — no pad exists between items unless written
// explicitly (the two HCZ2/DrumTest pads below are the ONLY such pads; every
// other adjacency in this section is genuinely zero-gap by construction,
// verified against the .asm: no OTHER member has a trailing `align`.
// song_table.asm's own trailing `align 2` — AFTER SongPatchTable_End — is
// deliberately dropped: a no-op at the current pins (both shapes' tails end
// even) and absorbed by main.asm's org-resume re-pin contract, which pins
// the post-bank resume address per shape anyway).
section mt_bank (cpu: m68000, bank: $8000) {
    data Song_MovingTrucks             = SongBlob
    data MovingTrucks_PitchTable_Stream = PitchBlob
    data MovingTrucks_Patches          = PatchesBlob

    // Sonic 2 EHZ + CPZ (every shape), each song then its own patch bank. The align-2
    // pads mirror HCZ2's self-adjusting one below: nothing here needs even addresses
    // (the Z80 reads bytes), but the section's other odd-length songs are padded, and
    // a pad that folds to nothing at an even length costs nothing. Today EHZ is even
    // (no pad) and CPZ odd (one $00).
    data Song_S2_EHZ    = S2EhzBlob
    data _s2_ehz_align  = if S2EhzBlob.len % 2 == 1 { byte(0) } else { Data.empty }
    data S2_EHZ_Patches = S2EhzPatchBlob
    data Song_S2_CPZ    = S2CpzBlob
    data _s2_cpz_align  = if S2CpzBlob.len % 2 == 1 { byte(0) } else { Data.empty }
    data S2_CPZ_Patches = S2CpzPatchBlob

    data Song_DrumTest = if DEBUG == 1 { DrumTestBlob } else { Data.empty }

    // song_drumtest.asm's trailing `align 2` mirrored explicitly (.emp never
    // auto-pads, §4.3): DrumTestBlob is 82 bytes (EVEN) at the current
    // pins, so this is a NO-OP today — folds to `Data.empty` — but it's
    // written as a SELF-ADJUSTING conditional (not simply omitted) so a
    // future DrumTest regeneration that lands on an ODD length stays
    // regen-safe without a human having to notice and add a pad by hand.
    // Only fires (emits one $00) when DEBUG == 1 AND the blob is odd-length.
    data _drumtest_align = if DEBUG == 1 && DrumTestBlob.len % 2 == 1 { byte(0) } else { Data.empty }

    data Song_HCZ2     = if DEBUG == 1 { Hcz2Blob }     else { Data.empty }

    // song_hcz2.asm's trailing `align 2` mirrored explicitly — CRITICAL for
    // byte-identity here (unlike the DrumTest pad above): Hcz2Blob is 6511
    // bytes (ODD) at the current pins, so asl's `align 2` inserts ONE real
    // $00 pad byte before `HCZ2_Patches` (reference ROM byte at $5D4A1 is
    // $00 — verified against the fact base). `.emp` sections never
    // auto-pad (§4.3), so this pad must be emitted EXPLICITLY, spelled as
    // a self-adjusting conditional (not a bare `byte(0)`) so a future HCZ2
    // regeneration that lands on an EVEN length correctly emits ZERO pad
    // bytes instead of silently drifting one byte off from the reference.
    // Only fires (emits one $00) when DEBUG == 1 AND the blob is odd-length
    // — today that's true, so this DOES emit the pin-critical byte.
    data _hcz2_align = if DEBUG == 1 && Hcz2Blob.len % 2 == 1 { byte(0) } else { Data.empty }

    data HCZ2_Patches  = if DEBUG == 1 { Hcz2PatchBlob } else { Data.empty }

    // --- SFX-base 8-alignment (package 3 fix, 2026-08-10) ---
    // The NEXT region in the sound bank (the SFX block, sfx_bank_blob.emp) must
    // start ≡ 0 (mod 8): the placement chainer 8-aligns that section's base,
    // while seam-2's sound_layout fold packs contiguously WITHOUT that align —
    // at a misaligned tail the two models diverge and every SfxTable pointer
    // cell + SfxBlobWinTab window pointer comes out short of the placed blobs
    // (observed: -2 after the 12-byte DacSample head growth made the tail
    // ≡ 2 mod 4 and plain SFX went silent; a mod-4-only pad still came out -4,
    // pinning the chainer's quantum at EIGHT — old working bases $5BAE8/$5D558
    // ≡ 0 mod 8 exclude 16). This pad closes the gap STRUCTURALLY: it is
    // emitted bytes inside the seam-2-lowered module, so the fold and the
    // chainer both count it, and the COMPTIME size (0-7 B, from this module's
    // own blob lengths) self-adjusts under song regen or shape change. NOT a
    // source `align`: seam-2 lowers this module at a baseline-0 section base,
    // so `align`'s pad count is computed against the wrong address whenever
    // the placed base is misaligned — its D2.29 congruence assert catches
    // that loudly (how this was learned). Instead the base IS forced ≡ 0
    // (mod 8) upstream (the dac_sample_tab.emp head-tail pad rounds the
    // engine-table head to 8, and the sound_bank map anchor is 8-aligned for
    // free — the placement rule aligns it to 0x8000), which ALSO makes the
    // baseline-0 comptime arithmetic here
    // exact. The pad is the section's last item, so it 8-aligns the section
    // END. seam-2 now predicts `Sfx_33` with the walk's own rounding (sigil
    // `native::packed_chained_base`), so what the pad still buys is that these
    // gap bytes are OURS (zeros in this section) rather than the map's fill,
    // and the SFX block does not move when a song's length changes parity.
    data _sfx_align = bytes(comptime for i in 0..MT_TAIL_PAD { 0 })
}
